-- TRIEL example inside the formal core: the notification of a personal data
-- breach to the supervisory authority, after Article 33 of the GDPR, as an
-- obligation with a fallback (WITHIN ... ELSE).
--
-- Durations count from the activation of the specification
-- (formal/core/CORE.md, section 8.3, point 5). Here the activation is the
-- moment when the controller became aware of the breach, so the controller
-- must notify the authority within 72 hours of it.
--
-- If it has not by then, the obligation is not breached: the fallback comes
-- into force at the first deadline, and a duration in its deadline counts from
-- that deadline (else_alt_duration). The notification with the reasons for
-- the delay is therefore due within 72 hours + 7 days of the activation, and
-- only a notification with reasons after the first deadline fulfils it
-- (else_alt_after).
--
-- The 7 days are an assumption of this example: Article 33 sets no such
-- period. It requires notification without undue delay and, where feasible,
-- within 72 hours, and a notification made later must give the reasons for
-- the delay.
--
-- Article 33 also exempts a breach that is unlikely to result in a risk to
-- the rights and freedoms of natural persons. That exemption needs a
-- conditional term whose branch has a deadline, which is outside the core:
-- the translator rejects a deadline in a composite term, and WITHIN ... ELSE
-- in a composite term (formal/core/CORE.md, section 10.6, rule 12), so the
-- exemption is not part of this example.
--
-- The SUBJECTS block declares the controller, the subject of the terms
-- (formal/core/CORE.md, section 9, decision 29), and the authority, which an
-- action argument may name only if it is declared (section 10.6, rule 9). No
-- factor comes from an ORACLE and there is no PENALTY, so neither
-- PROVENANCE_REQUIRED nor CURRENCY is required (decision 28). Every construct
-- in this file is translated into the Isabelle/HOL core (formal/core) and
-- evaluated by the exported evaluator (evaluator/).

SPECIFICATION gdpr_art33_notification VERSION 1.0.0
    JURISDICTION "EU"

SUBJECTS {
  controller : PARTY,
  authority  : REGULATOR
}

TERMS {
  controller MUST notify(authority) WITHIN 72 HOURS
    ELSE controller MUST notify_with_reasons(authority) BY 7 DAYS
}

FACTORS {
  affected_records : Integer METADATA SOURCE controller
}

INVARIANTS {
  records_known : LIVENESS : EVENTUALLY(PRESENT(affected_records))
}
